      <activity id="b2a03ce9-5d57-5ea0-926f-52be44bb27c8" activityNameId="3f8869cc-8f7f-5942-b4a0-7ee3036d3cc6" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Formic acid from butane, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Formic acid from butane, at plant
The multioutput-process "formic acid production, butane oxidation process"  delivers the co-products formic acid, methyl acetate, ethyl acetate, acetic acid, methyl ethyl ketone, and acetone. The allocation is based on mass balance.;
UUID: 27e4de09-da89-30cf-9e69-1f044dce95e2
Butane oxidation including materials, energy uses, infrastructure and emissions.
Location: The inventory is modelled for Europe.
Technology: Oxidation of butane
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: Transports and emissions are modelled with standard methods.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_27e4de09-da89-30cf-9e69-1f044dce95e2.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
